// PicoLCR_Sweep_v3_2.ino  
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Sweep + Goertzel single-bin DFT impedance measurement.
// Round-robin ADC -> FIFO -> DMA -> RAM capture path.
//
// 3.2 -- 
//
//   * CAPTURE PATH REWRITTEN. analogRead() is removed The ADC now "free-runs" in
//     round-robin mode over ADC0/ADC1 with the FIFO feeding a DMA channel that
//     writes straight into one interleaved buffer. CPU timing doesn't matter. 
//
//   * introduced proper adc overclocking with selectable profiles g1,g2,g3 etc or custom setting.
//
//   * SAMPLE RATE IS SCHEDULED PER POINT. New cfg.m_target holds samples per
//     cycle per channel roughly constant by varying the ADC divisor with
//     frequency, capped at the hardware ceiling.
//
//   * SINGLE INTERLEAVED BUFFER. DMA cannot scatter alternating samples into
//     two arrays, so buf_total[]/buf_dut[] are replaced by buf_rr[] and the
//     Goertzel / mean / saturation helpers take a stride and an offset. Same
//     total RAM (16 kB), one fewer copy.
//
//   * CAPTURE INTEGRITY CHECKED PER RECORD. FIFO over/underflow and the ADC's
//     post-capture AINSEL are both verified. An overflow slips channel parity
//     for the whole remainder of the buffer, which would otherwise look like a
//     180 degree phase bug rather than a dropped sample. See FLAG_ADC_ERR.
//
//   * 'y' COMMAND: channel-match self-test. Tie GP26 and GP27 to the same
//     buffered node. Ideally just after the gain stage from the AD9833 This separates capture-path error from
//     front-end error and is the test that validates the de-skew model.
//
// ==============================================
// TOPOLOGY (2-wire, hard-coded R_sense):
//
//   AD9833 out --+-- R_sense --+-- DUT --+-- GND
//                |             |
//              ADC0          ADC1
//            (V_total)      (V_DUT)
//
//   Z_DUT = R_sense * V_DUT / (V_total - V_DUT)      [complex]
//
// CAPTURE MEMORY LAYOUT:
//   buf_rr[0] = ADC0, buf_rr[1] = ADC1, buf_rr[2] = ADC0, ...
//   Channel A (V_total) is stride 2 offset 0. Channel B (V_DUT) is offset 1.
//   ADC1 is sampled ONE AGGREGATE PERIOD after its paired ADC0 sample.
//
// BUILD NOTES:
//   Board:  Raspberry Pi Pico W  (arduino-pico core by Earle Philhower)
//   CPU Speed: 192 MHz if the menu offers it. Otherwise setup() calls
//              set_sys_clock_khz(192000) itself. If neither succeeds the code
//              still runs -- it falls back to whatever clk_adc it ends up with
//              and derates the rate ceiling accordingly. Check 'k' output.
//
// SERIAL COMMANDS (115200 baud):
//   f<Hz>   excitation frequency (live mode)      m       toggle live monitor
//   a<Hz>   sweep start                          b<Hz>   sweep stop
//   p<Hz>   sweep step                           S       run sweep (q aborts)
//   d       re-dump last sweep from RAM          r<Ohm>  set R_sense
//   g<0|1|2> profile: fast / normal / precise
//   n<cyc>  target cycles per capture            v<M>    averages per point
//   c<spc>  target samples/cycle/channel         i<N>    record length floor
//   j<N>    record length ceiling                x<ms>   per-point time budget
//   e<ms>   settle after freq step               w       toggle Hann window
//   y       channel-match / skew self-test       t       timing breakdown
//   k       ADC + clock report                   u       raw dump of last capture
//   o<1|2|3> CLK_ADC_DIV: pll_sys / half / third
//                                                ?  settings    h  help
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

